    "details": "The rabbitmq-c project reports:\n\n> A malicious AMQP peer can trigger memory exhaustion in rabbitmq-c\n> clients by sending frames with unrecognised types or invalid channel\n> numbers. The client allocates per-channel memory pools and stores\n> complete frames before validating the channel against the negotiated\n> limits or the frame type, and discards unknown frames without\n> releasing that memory, allowing a sustained stream of small frames to\n> exhaust client resources.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0498",
